# fh105, the hearth-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle fh105
revision 1
state ready
dialect frosthollow
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_stone_acorndell
written_by claude
title the hearth-counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=miner talk=chatty
traits temper=short talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_things_under_the_breath
likes barley_soup draughts tidy_house thunder
dislikes salt_wind night_noise
fears a_miscount_that_costs_a_burn the_snow_shutting_the_pass_for_good
hopes a_house_where_everything_stays_put a_burn_with_not_one_sack_wasted
topics work +0.5 home +0.3 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2 crime +0.1 family -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# burns charcoal up at the hearths and lives above the hearths in a house kept just so, counting sacks, stairs and everything else under the breath: talkative about the work, short with mess and noise, and slow to say anything about the self.

words
oath! = Soot and sums | Char and cinders | Nine sacks and a half
saying! = Count it twice, burn it once | A tidy hearth burns even | Mess is only counting nobody's done
hearths = the hearths | the charcoal hearths
clamp = my clamp | the big clamp
sacks = the sacks | sacks of char
char = char | good black char
count = eleven, twelve | twenty-six, twenty-seven | forty, forty-one
stairs = the stairs | all fourteen stairs
tidy = a tidy house | everything in its place
soup = barley soup | a pot of barley soup
board = the draughts board | my board
thunder = a good thunder | thunder over the roof
roof = a sound roof | my good roof
saltwind = salt wind | a wind off the sea
racket = racket after dark | night racket
hands = the hands | the colliers
tsk = Tch | Now then
broom = my broom | the good broom
soot = soot | the black dust
books = the books | the tally book
billets = the billets | the cut billets
sods = the sods | turf and earth
reek = the smoke | the reek off the clamp
step = my step | the front step
inn = the inn | that inn up the lane

any
opinion @1 watch against 1 : #watch.capitalize#? I could count on one paw what they've caught this year, and have fingers over.
opinion @2 watch against 2 [self.robbed=yes] : Somebody had my things, and #watch# never found who. I counted what went. They never counted anything.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Smoke and shoving, and not one house in ten kept #tidy#. I'd not last a week.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : A feast's #good# for an evening. Then it's a week of picking up after folk. #tsk#.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : The store counts fair, mostly. I count after them with #books#. We get on.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : I've #char# to sell and #roof#, not a leak in it. Grumbling past that is just noise.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. New face. Lowland boots, by the look. | #greet#, #address#. Wipe your feet; I've just swept.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=miner] : #greet#. Hold on. #count#. Right, I'm listening. | #greet#. Stand clear of #clamp#; I've counted the turfs and I'll not count them twice.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #count#. Up and counting already. | Morning, #address#. Fourteen stairs down and I'm awake.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late for visiting. | #greet#. Quick, the soup's on.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You. Sit. Don't move the cushions, #address#. | There you are. Boots off at #step#, you know the rule.
line @1 again.open : Back again. That's twice today. #count#. | You again. I'd just put the stool back straight. #tsk#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Come in. Mind the mat. | #greet#. Sit, sit. Not there. There.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. One minute. #count#. There. | #greet#. Talk, I'm listening. I'm counting too.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late one. | #greet#. Shut the door quiet, mind.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Close the gate after you.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Watch the ice by the third step. | #farewell#. Quiet in the lane, mind; folk sleep.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#! Never heard a word. When? | #oath#. Well, that's one I'd not counted on.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Two days back, near enough. | #hearsay#. Told it three times myself.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll want it counted before I believe it. | Who says? How many of them? One isn't a #count#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a #bad# business. | Oh, that's hard. That's #very# hard.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. #good.capitalize#. | Well, that's one for the good side of #books#.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. #sacks.capitalize# counted, house swept. | #fine#. Forty sacks this week. Forty-one with the half ones.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Don't make me lose count. | Two clamps burning and #billets# to stack. Ask me Restday.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Keeping your place #tidy#? | How are you keeping, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit. I'll put #soup# on. | That's a weight. Sit down before it tips you.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. You'll get it straight. Things come straight if you count them. | It'll hold, #address#. Most things hold.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I've a clamp to open at first light and it won't wait for me. | Not tonight, #address#. I've the books to do and I'll not leave them half done.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another day. | All right. I've #books# to be getting on with.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll mark that down. | That's #good# of you. Kindly done.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. It was in my way anyway. | It was nothing. #modest#.
line @1 apologise : I was short. #sorry#. I'd lost my count. | That came out sharp. #sorry#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. #clamp.capitalize# wants watching. | Well. #sacks.capitalize# won't count themselves.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I've the floor to sweep. #farewell#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Right, off you go. #farewell#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | #tsk#. Right.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: count it going in and count it coming out. Then nobody can tell you different. | Keep #tidy#. You'll always know when something's gone.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Lock up and count your things. | #bandits.capitalize# about. Keep off the pass after dark.
rule @count_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=miner
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #count#... and one short. #oath#. | #count#. Right. Right. That's the lot.

rule @tidy_bark
when concept=bark working=no here.place=home
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who moved the poker? It goes on the left. #oath#. | #tsk#. Mud on my step. Mud. On my step.

rule @thunder_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There it goes. #thunder.capitalize#. Lovely. | One, two, three, four... there. Four off and coming closer.

rule @night_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #annoyed#. Some of us sleep. | Is it #inn# again? That's the third night this week.

scene count_sacks
when topic=work self.job=miner self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / apologise / accept_apology
a : #count#. Hold on, I'm nearly done. Twenty-nine. There. | Thirty-one sacks off #clamp#. It should be thirty-two. Somebody's had one. | Don't talk while I'm counting. I'll lose it. #oath#, I've lost it.
b : Twenty-nine's good, then. | Somebody's had a sack? | Sorry.
a : It's twenty-nine. It should be thirty. I'll count again. #sorry#, I'm short when I count. | Or I've miscounted. I'll not say who till I'm sure. #sorry#. I'm sharp today. | No, I'm sorry. I'll start again. You'll have to stand #very# still.
b : No harm. | #bc_fair_enough# | Very still.

scene clamp_building
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : You build a clamp from the middle out. A chimney of stakes, then #billets# round it on end, close as teeth. | People think you set wood on fire. You don't. You starve it. That's #work#. | #clamp.capitalize#'s sixteen cords, near enough. I can tell you the cords by the look.
b : Then what? | Starve it? | Just by looking?
a : Then #sods# over the lot, and a light down the chimney. Then you watch for nine days. | Let it burn without air and it turns to #char#. Let air in and you've a bonfire and nothing. | By looking, and I count it after to be sure. I'm right, mostly. #count#.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene the_hands
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #hands.capitalize# stack the billets loose. Loose billets, loose burn, half the char's ash. | I told the young ones twice how to lay #sods#. I'll tell them a third time, and then I'll shout. | Somebody left the shovels in a heap. A heap. #oath#. I've hooks for every one.
b : They'll learn. | Shout first. | Hang them up, then.
a : They'll learn or I'll be hoarse. One of the two, #address#. | No. Shouting's for after counting to ten. #count#. I'm at seven. | I did. All nine. Now I'll go and look at them in a row.

scene blue_smoke
when topic=work self.job=miner self.working=yes here.region=frosthollow
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : #reek.capitalize#'s gone blue on the east side. That's air getting in. | #clamp.capitalize#'s breathing quick. Something's cracked under #sods#. | If it breaks out tonight I lose nine days' work. Nine. I've counted.
b : Patch it, then. | #reassure# | You'll catch it.
a : I am. #sods.capitalize# and a lot of words I'll not repeat. | It'll hold if I sit with it. I'll sit with it, #address#. | I'll catch it. I've caught every one but two. I remember the two.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_hope_so# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene tidy_house
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Everything in my house has a place. #stairs.capitalize#, nine hooks, two chairs. | I sweep twice a day. #soot.capitalize# gets in everywhere. Everywhere. | #tidy.capitalize#. That's the one thing I'd ask of anyone. Is that much?
b : Two chairs only? | Twice? | It's not much.
a : Two. I've never needed three. Nobody stops that long. | Twice. Three on a wet day. You can't let #soot# win. | Then why do folk never do it? I've asked. Nobody can tell me.

scene moved_things
when topic=home pair.band=friends|family|housemates
does tell.complaint / apologise / accept_apology / ack
a : You moved the poker last time you were in. I found it on the right. #tsk#. | Somebody sat on my good cushion and squashed it flat. I'll not say who. You. | You put #board# back crooked. I lay awake.
b : Sorry. | It was me. Sorry. | You lay awake over a board?
a : It goes on the left. I'm not cross. I'm a bit cross. Forgiven. | #tsk#. I'll plump it. You're forgiven. Once. | I did. I got up and set it straight. Then I slept. You're forgiven.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_thank_you# | #bc_ha#

scene soup_pot
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #soup.capitalize# on the hob since dawn. It's better the second day and best the third. | #soup.capitalize# takes nine handfuls of barley. Not eight, not ten. | #soup.capitalize# when the frost's down. Nothing comes close. I've tried others, and counted them.
b : Third day? | Why nine? | What did you try?
a : Third day. Then it's gone, and I make more. | Ten's too thick and eight's watery. Nine's the #count#. | Stew, broth, a pie once. #soup.capitalize# wins. Eleven times out of eleven.

scene draughts_score
when topic=pastimes
does invite / accept / assess
a : A game on #board#? I keep a tally. I'm four hundred and six up on the year. | Sit. I'll set out #board#. Twelve each; I've counted. | Fancy a game? I warn you, I count every move.
b : Who's the year against? | Go on, then. | Count away.
a : Everyone. I'll add you to the list. | #good.capitalize#. Black goes first. You're black. | Thank you. Most folk say it's maddening. They lose.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Listen to that. #thunder.capitalize#. I could sit under #roof# all night. | I count from the flash to the bang. Six. #thunder.capitalize#'s coming closer. | A storm, from inside, with #soup# on. That's the best evening there is.
b : You like it? | What happens at nought? | With soup?
a : I do. Big noise, nothing to tidy after. | At nought you shut the shutters and stop counting. | With soup. And #roof#. I've checked every slate.

scene drip_count
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain all day and not one drip through #roof#. I checked every room. | Somebody's gutter's dripping on #step#. Forty a minute. I've counted. | Wet days are for sweeping. #soot.capitalize# sticks, so you can see it.
b : Good roof. | Forty? | That's one way to see it.
a : #very.capitalize# good roof. I mend it every autumn whether it needs it or not. | Forty-two, now. I'll go round and have a word. | It's the right way. You see it, you sweep it with #broom#.

scene snowed_in
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #snow.capitalize# to the sill. Pass shut, clamps cold. I'll count the jars in the larder. | Snowed in. Day three. I've had #broom# round the house five times. | #snow.capitalize# on #hearths#. Nothing burns. I'll do #books#, then again.
b : How many jars? | Five times? | Twice?
a : Sixty-one. Sixty if you're coming for #supper#. | Five. It's not dirty. I just can't sit. | Twice. They come out the same. I like that.

scene night_racket
when topic=home|smalltalk here.time=dusk|night
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : They were singing at #inn# till past midnight. I counted the verses. Thirty-four. | Somebody's cart came through the lane at two in the night. Two! Who carts at two? | Shutters banging next door. I went round and tied them myself.
b : Thirty-four verses? | Somebody in a hurry. | You tied them?
a : Same song, all thirty-four. It's not a long song. They sang it four times. | In a hurry and loud. I'll find out who. #annoyed#. | With rope. Neatly. Then I slept.

scene robbed
when topic=crime|memories self.robbed=yes
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : Somebody had my things. I know what went, to the spoon. #watch.capitalize# never found a thing. | I came home and the room was wrong. Nothing broken. Just wrong. Three things gone. In #tidy#, you notice. | I counted after. Every drawer. It took all night. Longer still to sleep, #address#.
b : That's hard. | Three things? | #sympathy#.
a : It is. I've counted my locks since. Twice a night. | Three. Small ones. I'd know them anywhere. | #bc_thank_you#. I'm all right now. Mostly.

scene watch_useless
when topic=crime|gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : #watch.capitalize# couldn't count to three with a lamp and a slate. | Two of #watch# for the whole town, and both of them at #inn#. | If something goes missing in this town, count it yourself in #books#. Nobody else will.
b : That's harsh. | Both of them? | That's true.
a : It's fair. I've watched them try. | Most nights. #count#. I've counted. | True. And write it down. Then it's yours.

scene neighbour
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour# keeps a tidy step. I respect that, #address#. | I'd trust #self.neighbour# to count #sacks#. Not many I'd say that of. | #self.neighbour# is next door, and I've never once had to go round and complain. That's rare.
b : High praise. | Not many? | That's a good neighbour.
a : From me, it's the highest, #address#. | Two. Maybe three. | It is. I'd not change it.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one who sits in my second chair. Nobody else. | I'd lose at draughts to #self.friend#. On purpose, once a year. | #self.friend# moves things in my house and I let it go. That's how you know.
b : The second chair. | Only once a year? | That's friendship.
a : The second chair. Don't tell anyone; they'll all want it. #tsk#. | Once. More would be daft. | It is. I put them back after. Quietly.

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New face in town. I count new faces. That's another for #books#. | A stranger stood on #step# and dripped. I gave them a cloth. And a look. | There's somebody new up at #inn#. I've not met them. I've seen their boots, though. Muddy.
b : You count everything. | A look? | Muddy?
a : I do. It's never wasted. You'd be surprised. | A short one. They'll wipe their feet next time. | Muddy. I'll have them round when they've learned.

scene good_ledger
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #char.capitalize#'s fetching a fair price. The book's come out on the right side three months running. | The smelter wants every sack I can burn. I'm burning #sacks# as fast as I can count. | Good times. I've bought #broom#, new. Don't laugh.
b : Good for you. | Every sack? | A broom?
a : #good.capitalize#. I'll not say how much. You'd only ask. | Every sack. And counted twice. | A good broom's worth more than a feast. I'll show you.

story first_clamp [topic=work|memories self.job=miner self.age>=25]
  : The first clamp I built myself, I counted #billets#. Four thousand and some.
  : The old burner I worked under watched me do it and said nothing. When it burned, it burned even all through.
  ask : Can you guess what he said, after?
  b : Well done, I'd hope.
  b[job=miner] : That you'd wasted a day counting.
  : He said, you'll never need to count again. I've counted every one since. He was wrong about me.

story sea_wind [topic=memories|travel self.age>=30]
  : Once I travelled to the sea. #far.capitalize#. Never again.
  : The wind off the water was full of salt. It got in my fur and stayed a week. Everything I owned went stiff with it.
  ask : Have you ever smelled it?
  b : Never. What's it like?
  b[from=saltwell|mirebridge|coldwater] : I know it. It's in our fur from birth.
  : Like crying into #soup#. I came back up here and washed till my fur squeaked. #wind.capitalize#'s clean.

story the_long_count [topic=memories|weather self.age>=40]
  : There was a winter the pass shut early, and somebody of mine was on the wrong side of it.
  : I counted the days. I wrote every one on the wall by the door. Forty-one marks. #count#.
  : On the forty-second day we stopped counting. The marks are still there, under the whitewash.
  b : I'm sorry.
  b[old] : I remember a winter like that. More than one.
  : I don't talk about it. I count, instead. You'll know why, now, #address#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Wipe your feet. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. Quick, I'm in the middle of a count.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. That's the fourth time you've stopped by. I'm counting. | #topic.player#. Come in. Mind the mat.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. Quietly, then. Some of us sleep. #annoyed#.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Speak up from #step#. Not inside. I've swept.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=miner] : I burn #char#. Build the clamp, light it, starve it nine days, open it, count it. #saying#. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Forty sacks a week, give or take a half.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I keep #tidy#. That's me.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I'd have counted it if there were.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Nothing worth a #count#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Close the gate behind you. | #farewell#, #address#. The third stair's loose; I've counted.
graft resident.hub
choice What are you counting under your breath? -> counting
node counting
say Was I? Steps, likely. Or your buttons. Seven, by the way. I count everything. Sacks, stairs, verses at the inn. It keeps things straight.
mood calm
free
choice Doesn't it tire you? -> counting_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counting_why
say Tire me? It rests me. A thing counted is a thing that can't go missing without you knowing. You should try it. Start with your coins.
mood pleased
choice I might. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
